% ============================================================================
% LatticeLang Bibliography
% ============================================================================
% Organized by topic.
% All entries are citable via :cite:p:`key` in any .rst file.
% Rendered by sphinxcontrib-bibtex in research/bibliography.rst.
%
% Tags:
%   % handchecked — entry info checked for accuracy by human against source
%   % book on shelf - owned first-hand
%   % downloaded - full paper in posession for cross-checking
%   % high — referenced multiple times in docs, priority to human-check
%   % unchecked — needs human verification before commit
%   % TODO — entry may be incomplete or placeholder
%
% Style:
%   - Author names: First Last
%   - Trailing commas: all fields except last line of each entry
%   - Address field is City only.
%   - Page ranges: use double-dash (283--333)
%
% Checks:
%   □ Go to the URL or DOI
%   □ Verify: author names, year, title spelling, venue/journal/booktitle, publisher, pages
%   □ For books: check edition number, ISBN if listed
%   □ For articles: confirm volume, issue, page range
%   □ Add `% verified YYYY-MM-DD via [source]` tag above the entry
%   □ If verification fails or URL is dead: mark `% TODO verify or remove`, don't delete yet
%   □ For entries without DOIs/URLs (shelf books): verify via Google Books or library catalog
%   ☐ Address vs. City — use just city (Cambridge, not Cambridge, UK).
%   ☐ Edition field — if not 1st edition, specify
%   ☐ Series field — some books belong to series
%   ☐ Note field overload — some entries have too much commentary in note. Keep it to bibliographic metadata; move prose to comments above entry.
%   ☐ Orphaned text after commas

Formatting:
%  - Consistent field ordering — alphabetical by key name, or grouped by topic.
%  - Trailing commas — all fields except last have trailing comma.
%  - Authors — First Last, reads clearer for the unfamiliar.
%  - Pages field — use -- double-dash en-dash for ranges.
%  - Month field — if known, add it (month = {may}). Often missing for books.
%  - ISBN/DOI/URL — if present, include.
%  - Comment prefixes
%  - Duplicate detection
%  - Entry type consistency
%
% ============================================================================


